      "body": "- [x] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n# What does this PR do?\n\nCheck the saver exit code after joining it and fail the conversion when the saver process fails. A real subprocess test writes to an invalid output path through the documented custom loader/saver plugin interface and previously returned zero despite NotADirectoryError.\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nSmall reproducible bug fix. No linked issue; no new feature or GPU kernel.\n\n## Reproduction and validation\n\n- Baseline `a21f8408d31322441c8401f119ee04b842aaad17`, using the real production module/CLI.\n- Before patch: **1 failed, 1 passed**. After patch: **2 passed**.\n- Focused CPU tests ran in a Linux container with Python 3.12.12 and PyTorch 2.8.0+cpu. Unrelated distributed/GPU suite fixtures were excluded with `--confcutdir=tests/unit_tests/tools/checkpoint`.\n- `tools/autoformat.sh` passed in check mode with Black26.3.0, isort5.13.2, Pylint3.2.6 and Ruff0.9.10; its non-gating mypy step also passed.\n- Full NVIDIA dev-container GPU unit and functional suites have not run. This PR remains a draft.\n\n## Pre-checks\n\n- [x] Added relevant focused unit regressions.\n- [ ] Added GPU functional tests.\n- [x] Ran the repository formatter in check mode.\n\nAI-assisted patch; the personal author-review checkbox remains unchecked pending the contributor's review.\n",
